WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.038 --> 00:00:05.711
That afternoon Nancy ran outside, urgently looking for Tom.

2
00:00:05.712 --> 00:00:09.558
The old man was in the barn cleaning harnesses.

3
00:00:09.559 --> 00:00:14.875
"You'll never guess who's sitting in the parlor," Nancy said breathlessly.

4
00:00:14.876 --> 00:00:19.780
"John Pendleton, and he's come to see Miss Polly!"

5
00:00:19.781 --> 00:00:26.320
Tom looked up from polishing a brass buckle. "You're joking."

6
00:00:26.321 --> 00:00:31.436
Nancy shook her head. "I let him in myself.

7
00:00:31.437 --> 00:00:37.097
And I've been meaning to tell you something: he was never Miss Polly's fiancé."

8
00:00:37.098 --> 00:00:39.401
"I know that."

9
00:00:39.402 --> 00:00:43.654
"Well, that story you told me made me think he was.

10
00:00:43.655 --> 00:00:52.564
Anyway, I found out Mr. Pendleton had been in love with Pollyanna's mother, Jennie, not Miss Polly."

11
00:00:52.565 --> 00:00:59.724
"That's right. He was the rich, older man Jennie's parents wanted her to marry."

12
00:00:59.725 --> 00:01:03.927
Nancy picked up a piece of straw, twirling it between two fingers.

13
00:01:03.928 --> 00:01:09.170
"I know Miss Polly didn't like Pollyanna's father because he took Jennie far away.

14
00:01:09.171 --> 00:01:15.256
But I still don't understand why Miss Polly and Mr. Pendleton dislike each other."

15
00:01:15.257 --> 00:01:20.466
"That goes back to a few years after Jennie got married."

16
00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:25.775
Tom handed Nancy the clean harness, and she hung it on the barn wall.

17
00:01:25.776 --> 00:01:33.027
"Miss Polly, who was 18 at the time, felt sorry for Mr. Pendleton.

18
00:01:33.028 --> 00:01:38.770
She made an effort to be extra nice to him." Tom paused.

19
00:01:38.771 --> 00:01:46.332
"Maybe she was too nice because some folks said she was chasing after him."

20
00:01:46.333 --> 00:01:52.806
"Knowing Miss Polly, I'd guess she was embarrassed by all that silly gossip."

21
00:01:52.807 --> 00:01:55.324
"Indeed she was.

22
00:01:55.325 --> 00:02:03.371
And this was around the time she broke off her own engagement, so folks were already talking about her.

23
00:02:03.372 --> 00:02:08.105
Mr. Pendleton wasn't too keen on the gossip either.

24
00:02:08.106 --> 00:02:17.176
After that, she shut herself up in this house, and he shut himself up in his house on Pendleton Hill."

25
00:02:17.177 --> 00:02:25.354
Tom started cleaning the leather of another harness with a wet rag. "So where's Miss Polly now?"

26
00:02:25.355 --> 00:02:31.221
"She was just coming downstairs when I ran out here."

27
00:02:31.222 --> 00:02:36.424
*** Mr. Pendleton attempted to rise from his chair as Aunt Polly entered the sitting

28
00:02:36.425 --> 00:02:39.861
room. Without shaking his hand, she took a

29
00:02:39.862 --> 00:02:44.983
seat. "I came to inquire about Pollyanna," Mr. Pendleton

30
00:02:44.984 --> 00:02:50.493
said. "Thank you, she's about the same," Aunt Polly replied

31
00:02:50.494 --> 00:02:54.991
sharply. "But how is she?" Mr. Pendleton pleaded for information.

32
00:02:54.992 --> 00:02:58.866
A quick spasm of pain crossed Aunt Polly's face.

33
00:02:58.867 --> 00:03:03.364
"I don't really have much information about her condition."

34
00:03:03.365 --> 00:03:06.008
"But surely the doctor—"

35
00:03:06.009 --> 00:03:09.954
"Dr. Warren himself seems baffled by this case.

36
00:03:09.955 --> 00:03:17.046
He's written to a specialist in New York, and that doctor has agreed to come here to examine Pollyanna."

37
00:03:17.047 --> 00:03:20.707
"Can you tell me anything about her injuries?"

38
00:03:20.708 --> 00:03:29.025
"A slight cut on the head, a few bruises, and damage to the spine that caused paralysis from the hips down."

39
00:03:29.026 --> 00:03:36.161
Mr. Pendleton moaned and was silent for a few moments.

40
00:03:36.162 --> 00:03:40.358
"How has Pollyanna reacted to being paralyzed?"

41
00:03:40.359 --> 00:03:47.687
"She doesn't seem to really understand, and I hesitate to say more to her until the specialist arrives.

42
00:03:47.688 --> 00:03:51.800
She's glad her legs are broken like your leg was.

43
00:03:51.801 --> 00:03:57.558
She doesn't want to be a lifelong invalid like Mrs. Snow."

44
00:03:57.559 --> 00:04:04.005
Through a blur of tears, Mr. Pendleton saw the pain in Aunt Polly's own eyes.

45
00:04:04.006 --> 00:04:09.372
He remembered how Pollyanna had said she couldn't leave Aunt Polly.

46
00:04:09.373 --> 00:04:12.855
And this made him decide to confess something to her.

47
00:04:12.856 --> 00:04:17.265
"I recently tried to get Pollyanna to come live with me," he said.

48
00:04:17.266 --> 00:04:21.743
"I thought I would adopt her and make her my heir."

49
00:04:21.744 --> 00:04:24.756
At this point Aunt Polly stopped listening.

50
00:04:24.757 --> 00:04:29.980
She thought about what a brilliant future Pollyanna would have with Mr. Pendleton.

51
00:04:29.981 --> 00:04:33.169
He had so much more money than she did.

52
00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:39.610
Then Aunt Polly remembered Pollyanna's saying that she loved being called "dear" by someone who belonged to her.

53
00:04:39.611 --> 00:04:46.125
And Aunt Polly thought about how dreary her own future would be without Pollyanna in the house.

54
00:04:46.126 --> 00:04:50.705
"How did Pollyanna respond to that?" Aunt Polly said harshly.

55
00:04:50.706 --> 00:04:57.165
"She said she wanted to stay with you." Mr. Pendleton pulled himself to his feet.

56
00:04:57.166 --> 00:05:00.858
"And she thought you wanted her to stay."

57
00:05:00.859 --> 00:05:05.189
Without looking at Aunt Polly, he headed for the front door.

58
00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:08.529
But he heard Aunt Polly by his side.

59
00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:16.661
"When the specialist comes and I know something definite, you'll hear from me."

60
00:05:16.662 --> 00:05:21.122
Aunt Polly slipped her trembling hand into Mr. Pendleton's.

61
00:05:21.123 --> 00:05:30.309
"Good-bye and thank you for coming. Pollyanna will be pleased to know you were here."

